<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Ross</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Ross was a Russian settlement on the coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-american-company">Russian-American Company</a> in 1812. It was meant to grow food for the Alaskan colonies and to hunt sea otters, but it never became profitable and was sold to John Sutter in 1841. It is now a state historic park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-ross.jpg" alt="Fort Ross" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frank Schulenburg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russian_chapel_at_Fort_Ross_(2016).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
